      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-11T13:00:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So rather than using a node label, it is better to use something like\nDT_COMPAT_GET_ANY_STATUS_OKAY(intel_ap_pwrseq_signal_list).\nOr use the DT_INST macro.\nAlso put in a check to verify there is only one node defined for this\ncompatible using something like:\n\n#if DT_HAS_COMPAT_STATUS_OKAY(intel_ap_pwrseq_signal_list)\nBUILD_ASSERT(DT_NUM_INST_STATUS_OKAY(intel_ap_pwrseq_signal_list) \u003d\u003d 1,\n             \"Only one node for intel_ap_pwrseq_signal_list is allowed\");\n#endif",
