        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-11T13:00:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are 2 ways to considerably simplify the mapping of which signal\nsourced the interrupt:\n1)\nUse the CONTAINER_OF() macro to map the callback to the containing structure:\n\n   struct power_signal_gpio_info {\n       enum power_signal signal;\n       ...\n       struct gpio_callback intr_cb;\n       ..\n   };\n   \n   ...\n   [in interrupt]\n   \n        struct power_signal_gpio_info *info;\n        \n        info \u003d CONTAINER_OF(cb, struct power_signal_gpio_info, intr_cb);\n        \n2)\nStore all of the interrupt callback structures in a single array, and use pointer arithmetic to get the index into the array:\n\n    struct gpio_callback intr_callbacks[POWER_SIGNAL_COUNT];\n    \n    ....\n        int power_signal;\n        \n        power_signal \u003d cb - \u0026intr_callbacks[0];\n        pwr_info \u003d \u0026power_signals[power_signal];",
      "revId": "524a8d1e50f3a1374a3cd3403b4406552039b80e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
